% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `common_network`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of
% `common_network` is printed or held, and NO NETWORK IS MODELLED.  Its one
% method is INTERPOLATED (labelled) from:
%   - pimfep##remote_stream's class methods create_from_fep/4,
%     create_to_fep/3, create_from_remote_fep/4 and
%     create_to_remote_fep/5, and remote_pimfep_invoker goal/1 (held
%     .ptf): each sends `:is_installed(#common_network)` first and goes on
%     to `:assign(#library)` and the stream's creation.  No clause of these
%     methods handles a network that is not installed: on failure the
%     method fails;
%   - docs/simpos/required/classes.tsv (row `common_network`): referenced
%     only by pimfep and pimmcsp, no other selector.
% Model (OURS): is_installed/1 succeeds.  The choice follows the callers,
% which are written for a FEP whose network is installed; it is not
% evidence that any network runs here.

class common_network has

% INTERPOLATED from: the remote_stream call sites (see above).  OURS: it
% succeeds.
:is_installed(Class);

end.
